  "justification": "Rationale A seriously misapplies the rubric by misclassifying the inferred action of adding missing details as an explicit action stated in the comment. Its core claim of explicit action is unsupported by the evaluated text, leading to an incorrect score. While it correctly identifies the concrete issues noted, it fails on the key rubric distinction between explicit and implicit action. Rationale B correctly interprets and applies the rubric: the action of adding clarifications is implicit (inferred from noting missing details) but concrete (specific sections and problematic notations are clearly identified, so authors know exactly what to fix), which correctly fits the criteria for score 4. All of B's claims are grounded in the provided material and fully justify the scoring decision."
